<title>HUNGARY: FORECAST - HUNGARY T-BILL YIELDS SEEN DROPPING.</title>
<headline>FORECAST - HUNGARY T-BILL YIELDS SEEN DROPPING.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungarian discount Treasury</p>
<p>bill are seen dropping at this weeks auctions following the</p>
<p>government's decision to cut the monthly crawling peg</p>
<p>devaluation rate to 1.1 percent from 1.2 on April 1, dealers</p>
<p>said on Monday.</p>
<p>Dealers' opinions about how bond yields will change at this</p>
<p>week's auctions were mixed.</p>
<p>The Government Debt Management Agency will auction</p>
<p>one-month T-bills on Tuesday, three-month T-bills on Wednesday,</p>
<p>three-year government bonds of the 2000/D series and seven-year</p>
<p>bonds of the 2004/F series on Thursday.</p>
